# /etc/udev/rules.d/40-ot2-usb-ethernet-cdrom-fix.rules
# Recovered from the first OT-2 camera Pi on 2026-11-10; written for byu-vcl PR 60 (2026-08-10).
# Only needed if the robot is cabled through a USB-Ethernet adapter (RTL8153). With the robot's
# cable in the Pi's built-in eth0, as ../ot2-link.md recommends, this rule never fires.
#
# The RTL8153 sometimes enumerates in its fake driver-CD mode (0bda:8151, USB mass storage)
# after a reboot or replug, so no eth1 appears. Eject + reset flips it to NIC mode (0bda:8153);
# the r8152 driver then binds and the ot2-usb NetworkManager profile connects.
# Needs: sudo apt-get install -y usb-modeswitch
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTR{idVendor}=="0bda", ATTR{idProduct}=="8151", RUN+="/usr/sbin/usb_modeswitch -v 0bda -p 8151 -K -R"
